# Bytes a rule of ours names by address, laid down by tools/rules/consts.py
# into delta_authored_enus.c and recorded in rules/symbols. See the top of
# that tool for what the bytes are: not ASCII, but one code per character in
# the alphabet the statement type declares.
#
# This one is IBM's own two-byte prefix "re" as ZZstring278 holds it, copied
# so that every build compiles a store of ours, registers it in the arena
# beside the lifted ones and copies it in. Nothing names it: what it proves is
# the path, on every build and in every configuration the suite runs. What
# proves the naming is in docs/building.md, which says how to hold a rule that
# reads this against the same rule reading IBM's copy.

bytes lex_prefix_re 18 02

